{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "050P", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\n\\mathcal{X} \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{Y} \\ar[r] &\n\\mathcal{Y}\n}\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-monomorphism-cartesian-square-inertia}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0737d65ba56fbde8514cac6fe8438efcd4a7917346d33d5a7e5bb5b7acbec9e7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7c7df7fe970eef9c3b4a800221453f528e3369ea42eeeeea0b00d0c6509f2032", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a monomorphism of algebraic stacks.\nThen the diagram\n<MATH_0002>\nis a fibre product square.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2bbc318072f68c39e4844f6f5a2eb03991aa5f3cdfb902e12f822f6bf008ba87", "unit_id": "tag:06R5:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "050P", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$T$", "MATH_0004": "$(x, \\alpha)$", "MATH_0005": "$x$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0007": "$T$", "MATH_0008": "$\\alpha : x \\to x$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0010": "$T$", "MATH_0011": "$f$", "MATH_0012": "$\\alpha$", "MATH_0013": "$\\beta : f(x) \\to f(x)$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0015": "$T$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0017": "$T$", "MATH_0018": "$((y, \\beta), x, \\gamma)$", "MATH_0019": "$y$", "MATH_0020": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0021": "$T$", "MATH_0022": "$\\beta : y \\to y$", "MATH_0023": "$\\mathcal{Y}_T$", "MATH_0024": "$\\gamma : y \\to f(x)$", "MATH_0025": "$T$", "MATH_0026": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{Y} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0027": "$T$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-lemma-monomorphism}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{categories-section-inertia}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3bf81ba4513e7f151e826c390c12b74e8ea29bb2499ad215c671663e42d1e463", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:eb85ecc11edefa554602174a5e54badbc8998b62a18866af41a2309e025e67a0", "source_text": "This follows immediately from the fact that <MATH_0001> is fully faithful (see\nProperties of Stacks, Lemma <REF_0001>)\nand the definition of the inertia in\nCategories, Section <REF_0002>.\nNamely, an object of <MATH_0002> over a scheme <MATH_0003> is\nthe same thing as a pair <MATH_0004> consisting of an object\n<MATH_0005> of <MATH_0006> over <MATH_0007> and a morphism <MATH_0008> in\nthe fibre category of <MATH_0009> over <MATH_0010>. As <MATH_0011> is fully faithful\nwe see that <MATH_0012> is the same thing as a morphism\n<MATH_0013> in the fibre category of <MATH_0014> over <MATH_0015>.\nHence we can think of objects of <MATH_0016> over <MATH_0017>\nas triples <MATH_0018> where <MATH_0019> is an object of\n<MATH_0020> over <MATH_0021>, <MATH_0022> in <MATH_0023> and\n<MATH_0024> is an isomorphism over <MATH_0025>, i.e., an object\nof <MATH_0026> over <MATH_0027>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0434d49d82222317f388d4c37d32cd952d5e2501adeaf37719e4cb3658ec280a", "unit_id": "tag:06R5:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "050P", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$[U/R] \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$G/U$", "MATH_0004": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nG \\ar[d] \\ar[r] & U \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{X}\n}\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-presentation-inertia}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:979b18971a8b211b77b9b541ebea54c196577b5e6214e5b4473aace33ec5cd58", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f41035b7a5dfec6af2887dca1ff78f1eeaae8acdde78bdb83a84e623adb1038b", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack. Let <MATH_0002>\nbe a presentation. Let <MATH_0003> be the stabilizer group algebraic space\nassociated to the groupoid <MATH_0004>. Then\n<MATH_0005>\nis a fibre product diagram.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1e262340bea58873067fd66cc7508298d9edf11e7b1b416ed0b78c339ccccf10", "unit_id": "tag:06PR:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "050P", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-groupoids-lemma-2-cartesian-inertia}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0d62b021aa2c00d37a4f737b36b785b392ebd037990919aa676ddad2332b94c8", "source_text": "Immediate from\nGroupoids in Spaces, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a58037640767527768099e708d185bd6066eb431cbe6ed7869f7a2fa50001c10", "unit_id": "tag:06PR:proof"}
